:SetTCCBehaviorOptions

        rem moved to environment-common-vars ➜ set TCC=c:\tcmd

        rem Make Ctrl-C/^C  and Ctrl-Break/^Break actually work!
                on break cancel
    
        rem The test:
        rem         1) run `grep "👽" <con:`         to get an emoji in the tasklist
        rem         2) run `tasklist /L | grep grep` to see if the grep works and the emoji displays properly

                rem Surprisingly, this was not how to get the result I wanted:
                        rem option //unicodeoutput=yes

                rem More surprisingly, this was:
                        rem moved to environment-common-vars: set UnicodeOutputDefault=no
                        rem moved to environment-common-vars:set    UTF8OutputDefault=yes
                        
                rem Some aliases for those variables:
                        rem moved to environment-common-vars:set DefaultUnicodeOutput=%UnicodeOutputDefault%
                        rem moved to environment-common-vars:set    DefaultUTF8Output=%UTF8OutputDefault%

                rem Actually set the optins to our default values:                                
                        option //UnicodeOutput=%UnicodeOutputDefault%
                        option //UTF8Output=%UTF8OutputDefault%

                rem NOTE: Setting these options in the TCC INI file works, but only if you set them in the [4NT] section of the INI
return





